{%- comment -%}
  The site's fonts: EB Garamond for headings and Inter for text, the owner's
  choice on 2026-09-14 (option D of the comparison in CLAUDE.md).

  Loaded from the theme's own files, not Shopify's font library. Every font file
  Shopify hosts is Latin-only, so with a library font each Bulgarian word fell
  back to the visitor's system fonts (Times New Roman and Arial on Windows).
  These files are the originals from Google Fonts, SIL Open Font License, split
  by alphabet. unicode-range lets the browser download only the parts a page
  uses, usually the upright Cyrillic and Latin files, about 140 KB in all.

  The family names end in "Theme" so they can never be matched to a Shopify
  library copy of the same font, which would have no Cyrillic.

  Rendered in the head of layout/theme.liquid, layout/password.liquid and
  templates/gift_card.liquid, after Dawn's :root block, whose font variables
  it overrides. The Typography font pickers in the theme editor no longer
  change the fonts; the size sliders still work.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- comment -%}theme-check-disable AssetPreload{%- endcomment -%}
<link rel="preload" as="font" href="{{ 'font-inter-normal-cyrillic.woff2' | asset_url }}" type="font/woff2" crossorigin>
<link rel="preload" as="font" href="{{ 'font-inter-normal-latin.woff2' | asset_url }}" type="font/woff2" crossorigin>
<link rel="preload" as="font" href="{{ 'font-eb-garamond-normal-cyrillic.woff2' | asset_url }}" type="font/woff2" crossorigin>
<link rel="preload" as="font" href="{{ 'font-eb-garamond-normal-latin.woff2' | asset_url }}" type="font/woff2" crossorigin>
{%- comment -%}theme-check-enable AssetPreload{%- endcomment -%}

<style>
  /* EB Garamond, italic, cyrillic */
  @font-face {
    font-family: "EB Garamond Theme";
    font-style: italic;
    font-weight: 400 600;
    font-display: swap;
    src: url({{ 'font-eb-garamond-italic-cyrillic.woff2' | asset_url }}) format("woff2");
    unicode-range: U+0301, U+0400-045F, U+0490-0491, U+04B0-04B1, U+2116;
